<http://data.silknow.org/object/8675ebe9-0457-3385-8c2b-729cfe14a131/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel/Napkin borders joined together, striped silk embroidered with silk in double darning, double running in a line and hem stitch, and with plate in satin stitch. Each border contains two complete and two partial motifs place between the stripes: the complete motif consists of a curved blue fish from whose mouth grows a large floral arrangment with a serrated blue leaf and pink flowers; the partial motif is actually a slim sprig with blue heart-shaped leaves and pink flowers."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8675ebe9-0457-3385-8c2b-729cfe14a131> .

